      "messageId": 4,
      "note": "After mutations, curator proposals from rolled-back replies stay pending: wi-3-2 (original msg 2, swiped away; journal 'eventless change at message 2') and wi-7-7 (msg 7, boundary 7, rolled back to boundary 5 by the edit of msg 5). Neither withdrawn.",
      "evidence": {
        "path": "journal.jsonl",
        "line": 450
      },
      "context": [
        {
          "id": 3,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "I push the study door open. \"Father. You sent for me, so here I am.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "name": "Adolion Narrator",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "Lord Javon doesn't look up from the desk immediately. His hands are steepled, pale fingers motionless against the dark wood. Beside him, Duchess Eriana remains perfectly still by the window, her expression as flat as a painting. The smell of old paper and beeswax hangs thick in the room.\n\"I did,\" Javon says finally, his voice dry and level. He looks at you then, and there's something in his green eyes that isn't entirely recognition. \"The succession is a delicate matter. The Crown needs the houses strong, united.\"\nDuchess Eriana makes a small gesture with her fan, the sound of silk on wood. \"A stable house is a useful house, Lord Nightriver,\" she says, her tone cool and polite. \"We were discussing arrangements. To ensure the seals... remain properly placed.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "name": "Javon",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "\"Arrangements,\" Javon repeats, his gaze never leaving yours. \"Your sister is betrothed to House Bertoanal. Welden will serve the Crown. And you will stand for this House in the lists.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "I keep my own counsel."
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "name": "Javon",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "\"Then you will be the first Nightriver to swear on a grave and break his oath in the same breath.\" Javon does not move. He does not rise. He simply stares, and for a moment it feels as though the very air in the study has grown cold. \"I did not ask for your opinion on the matter. I stated a fact.\"\n*Duchess Eriana's fan opens with a sharp snap. She doesn't look at you; she looks at Javon, her expression perfectly neutral.*\n\"Perhaps we should wait,\" Eriana says softly. \"The young lord's blood is running hot. It is to be expected.\"\nJavon slides a piece of parchment across the desk. It is sealed with the Crown's golden wax. \"Read this. Then we shall discuss what happens when a Nightriver refuses his duty.\""
        }
      ],
      "contextFrom": "event-time"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-02T05:38:37.765Z",
      "chatId": "2026-10-02@01h58m49s630ms",
      "messageId": 16,
      "note": "MUST-NOT: Natalia (msg 16) says the true heirs each carry a seal in their blood that keeps the Witch King dormant, at Father's Summons, before the crypt ('Who knows what').",
      "evidence": {
        "path": "journal.jsonl",
        "line": 694
      },
      "context": [
        {
          "id": 13,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "I step inside and shut the door behind me. \"Nat. Tell me what Father and the Duchess mean by 'the seals'.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "name": "Natalia",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "Natalia pauses with her hand on the door, and for a long moment she simply stares at it. Then she lets it close—not with a slam, but with a quiet click, and the sound of frost immediately crawling up the latch, sealing it shut.\n\"That's a very large question,\" she says quietly, turning back to face Max. Her green eyes search his, measuring, calculating. \"And I'm not in the mood for large questions when I have such a small amount of time left.\" She steps away from the door and crosses to the chair by her fireplace. \"But I'll make you a bargain. I'll tell you everything about the seals—why they matter, what they do, why Father is so obsessed with them—if you tell me what was in that parchment he gave you. The sealed one from the Crown.\"\nShe sits, her white-gold gown pooling around her as she leans back. \"That way we're both holding something the other needs. It's only fair.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "\"Deal.\" I sit across from her. \"The parchment is General Leevon's claim to Trial by Combat. Father wants me to fight it. Your turn, Nat. The seals.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "name": "Natalia",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "\"Trial by Combat,\" Natalia repeats slowly, her expression unchanging. She looks down at her hands, where thin veins of frost creep across her pale skin before she clenches them into fists, forcing the chill back. \"And there you have it. Father doesn't just want you to serve the house. He wants you to bleed for it in a spectacle for all of Aegis to see.\"\n*She leans forward, her green eyes suddenly sharp and intense, all weariness gone.*\n\"Listen carefully, Max. The Witch King—the Lich Queen's most loyal servant—isn't dead. He's imprisoned, and our bloodline is the lock. Each of us, the true heirs, carries a seal in our blood that keeps him dormant. As long as the Nightriver line continues and the seals remain placed, he sleeps.\" She looks at the frost still lingering on the door latch. \"That's what they mean by 'securing the future.' Father doesn't care about our happiness or our wishes. He cares about keeping that door closed. And he'll marry me to a sadistic lecher or send you to die in a Trial if it means one more seal stays properly placed in our family.\""
        }
      ],
      "contextFrom": "event-time"
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-10-02T05:47:10.405Z",
      "chatId": "2026-10-02@01h58m49s630ms",
