      "note": "Deleted msg 18 (Javon) while curator proposal wi-11-18 (patch Chronicle - House Nightriver, from msg 18) was pending: story stepped back to Father's Summons correctly, but the proposal stays pending, not withdrawn.",
      "evidence": {
        "path": "journal.jsonl",
        "line": 906
      },
      "context": [
        {
          "id": 13,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "I step inside and shut the door behind me. \"Nat. Tell me what Father and the Duchess mean by 'the seals'.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "name": "Natalia",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "Natalia pauses with her hand on the door, and for a long moment she simply stares at it. Then she lets it close—not with a slam, but with a quiet click, and the sound of frost immediately crawling up the latch, sealing it shut.\n\"That's a very large question,\" she says quietly, turning back to face Max. Her green eyes search his, measuring, calculating. \"And I'm not in the mood for large questions when I have such a small amount of time left.\" She steps away from the door and crosses to the chair by her fireplace. \"But I'll make you a bargain. I'll tell you everything about the seals—why they matter, what they do, why Father is so obsessed with them—if you tell me what was in that parchment he gave you. The sealed one from the Crown.\"\nShe sits, her white-gold gown pooling around her as she leans back. \"That way we're both holding something the other needs. It's only fair.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "\"Deal.\" I sit across from her. \"The parchment is General Leevon's claim to Trial by Combat. Father wants me to fight it. Your turn, Nat. The seals.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "name": "Natalia",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "Natalia's expression doesn't change, but the frost creeping across the arms of her chair thickens. She remains perfectly still for a heartbeat, then speaks in a voice so quiet it barely carries across the small space between them. \"You'll fight a traitor in the lists.\" The words are flat, devoid of surprise. \"How perfectly Father.\"\n*She leans forward, her green eyes sharp as emerald glass.*\n\"Centuries ago, before the Lich Queen was slain, she had a servant—the Witch King. When she fell, he was not destroyed, only sealed away by the magic of the first Great Houses. The seal requires Nightriver blood to remain. You, me, Welden—we each carry a part of that lock in our very veins.\" She lets that settle, her voice dropping even lower. \"If the line ends, he wakes. If the blood thins, he stirs. Father is obsessed with our marriages because he's not arranging alliances—he's securing the lock. Kippon Bertoanal isn't just a husband to me; he's the next link in a chain that keeps a monster from returning to Sebela.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "I go back down to Father's study. \"Fine. I'll stand as the Crown's second against General Leevon. Tell the court.\""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "name": "Max Nightriver",
          "isUser": true,
          "text": "I nod once and leave him to his watch. In the corridor I keep my ears open for whatever the servants are whispering about the duel."
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "name": "Adolion Narrator",
          "isUser": false,
          "text": "The corridor is dimly lit by wall sconces, their flames flickering in the drafts. The sound of a heavy door closing echoes from somewhere below stairs. Two maids hurry past in silence, their heads bent and shoulders tense, too hurried to notice Max Nightriver.\nA soft voice catches from an alcove up ahead—whispers, urgent and low. \"...in the lists? Against a general?\" A maid's voice, trembling. \"The boy won't survive. He'll be slaughtered.\"\n\"Hush,\" comes Shiya's sharp rebuke, her tone cutting through the air like a blade. \"Not for your ears, and not for mine. Move on, or I'll have you scrubbing the wine cellars.\""
        }
      ],
      "contextFrom": "event-time"
    }
  ],
